<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23892" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sōlo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		in-sol, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to place in the sun</i>, i. e. <i>expose to the sun</i>, in order to warm, dry, etc. (a favorite
			word with Columella): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uvas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 39, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insolati dies,</span>”
				<i>sunny</i>, <i>sunshiny days</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 3, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humus insolatur,</span>”
				<i>becomes warmed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					4, 17, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
